Description: Provides tools for robust differential item functioning (DIF)
    analysis in two-group item response theory models. The package computes
    item-level scaling functions, estimates robust scaling parameters via
    iteratively reweighted least squares with Tukey's bisquare loss, and
    supports Wald-type tests for item-level and aggregate impact differences.
    Inputs can be supplied directly from model parameter/covariance objects or
    extracted from fitted 'mirt' and 'lavaan' models. Methods are described in
    Halpin (2022) <https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.04598>.
